Bukiyip (also called Mountain Arapesh; ISO 639-3 ape) is a Torricelli (Arapesh) language of East Sepik Province, Papua New Guinea, spoken between Yangoru and Maprik. It has an elaborate noun-class system. It should not be confused with Abelam (Ambulas), a Ndu language.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found in the search results.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Conrad and Wogiga, \emph{An Outline of Bukiyip Grammar} (Pacific Linguistics C-113, 1991), listed in the ANU repository under CC BY 4.0: \url{https://openresearch-repository.anu.edu.au/items/d4478933-b15f-4283-a54f-8ceb6ce28c89}
\item Bukiyip word list in the ASJP database: \url{https://asjp.clld.org/languages/BUKIYIP}
\item Overview article: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bukiyip_language}
\end{itemize}
No dedicated dictionary was found.

